        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The crowd wanted a getaway sweep; instead, the ninth inning turned into a gut punch. <strong>The Cardinals dropped four runs in the top of the ninth and handed Toronto a 5-1 loss on Aug. 2, snapping the Jays' brief roll and leaving them at 52-60, fifth in the AL East, 13.5 games back.</strong> That is the blunt truth of this club now - a team that can string together a few clean nights, then cough up the late leverage when it matters most. The good news is the bats showed life in the previous two wins over St. Louis, but the margin for error is paper-thin and the season math is grim. Kevin Gausman's trade to the Cubs has only sharpened the sense that this is a roster in transition. <strong>Next comes Houston tonight - and the Astros will make Toronto earn every inch.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated August 3, 2026"
