      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "The building is quiet, and that is the point in August - nothing to do now but wait on the one matter hanging over the roofline. <strong>The Kawhi Leonard trade remains on ice while the NBA investigation drags on</strong>, and Toronto's summer is being shaped more by uncertainty than by movement. The Raptors sit at 3rd in the Atlantic Division, but that final ledger is only a snapshot; the real issue is roster construction, not last winter's numbers. Fans want a cleaner answer in the front office, and they want to know whether Scottie Barnes' open-threes growth is real or still a promise. If Leonard does arrive for camp in Quebec City, the whole picture changes. <strong>For now, the watchword is patience - until the investigation breaks, everything else is just wallpaper.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated August 3, 2026"
      },
